     1,
     "Hello I use the ggplot package. With the new version I am facing the\r<br>following issue. Can you assist?\r<br>\r<br>Error in continuous_scale(aesthetics, &quot;date&quot;, identity, breaks =\r<br>breaks, :\r<br>unused argument(s) (format = &quot;%d-%b-%y&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>Regards\r<br>\r<br>=\r<br>\r<br>This is the answer I received from R studio. This indeed is a problem\r<br>that appears when using RGUI.\r<br>\r<br>=\r<br>\r<br>Mukul,\r<br>\r<br>This sounds like more of an R problem than about RStudio. Does this\r<br>same error occur when just using RGui? If so you might want to try\r<br>posting to the ggplot2 mailing list:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375987717000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Wn1bYLQKPzuvQeY8uoogk\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a>\r<br>\r<br>Josh"
    ]
   ]
