  {
   "id": "cZV9UYhoVeAJ",
   "from": "Dennis Murphy",
   "author": "0c39e60ddb38622b",
   "date": "2012-04-30T12:26:22Z",
   "subject": "Re: GGplot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi:\r<br>\r<br>It may be worth reading certain portions of the ggplot2-0.9.0\r<br>transition guide - in particular, section 7.1 on dates and datetimes.\r<br>It&#39;s probably worth going over section 6 as well to get some sense of\r<br>how the scales package is used for date, datetime and transformed\r<br>scales in this version. If you still have trouble after reading the\r<br>aforementioned material, please provide a reproducible example\r<br>containing both data and code.\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"http://bit.ly/AhLHuV\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bit.ly/AhLHuV&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375987718000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bRNPgbFpDFWDmi0vAoDea\">http://bit.ly/AhLHuV</a>\r<br>\r<br>HTH,\r<br>Dennis\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
